        "spans_beyond_this_verse": true,
        "translator": "K. M. K. Murthy / Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
        "text": "\"Even Seetha, daughter-in-law of Dasaratha, and Rama's beloved wife equalling to Rama's life, ever well disposed, born in the family of Janaka and one as though fashioned by a Divine marvel, endowed with all good characteristics and the best among women, followed Rama to forest, like Rohini following the Moon... [1-1-26b, 27, 28a]"
      }
